# Google I/O '25 Developer Keynote - Audio Described

* labs.google/stich - tool to generate app designs that can be exported to figma files
* Google AI studio - tool for building apps with AI
* Google GenAI SDK now supports MCP
* Androidify - app build with AI model available with the Firebase SDK
* On-device AI - lets you process prompts locally, without sending data to a server, powered by GenAI API called Gemini Nanom 
* Live updates - new in Android 16, lets you show time-sensitive updates for things like navigation, deliveries, ride shares. It uses a new progress style template
* Changes in android 16 - Changes in the android API will apps to no longer react to orientation, resizability and aspect ratio restrictions, basically this change will be made to force apps to be adaptive saying goodbye to "mobile-only" apps this will force apps to be responsive by default, for this you can leverage the "compose adaptive layouts" library you can us things like "pane expansion" and all apps will be automatically available for android tablets, foldables, cars(you'd have to opt-in into distribution via Play Console and making minor optimization) and XR
* Android XR SDK - SDK for building for Android XR
* Newest Jetpack Compose release includes features like: autofill, text autosize, visibility tracking, Accessibility checks, animate Bounds, contentReceiver, Ellipsis, HTML formatting, State-based TextField, Camera X, media 3, navigation(built from ground up again)
* Journeys: Natural language tool to write end-to-end test(autometed test) available in android studio, they are commonly implemented using espresso, but now you can create "xml" files inside your test source set
* Update Depencendies: Gemini in Android Studio can help you update them now however you may need build catalogs, option available under "Refactor>Update Dependencies", this is powered by gemini

## Web Apps
new features in chrome to build better UI debug a your websites more easily with devtools and AI features more quickly with Gemini Nano in Chrome

* Carrousels in pure HTML and CSS: Stylable Fragmentation, Scroll maker elements, Scroll Buttons
* Rich Tootips, Preview Cards/Hover cards and hint UI could be replaced with experimental APIs called "interest Invoker", "Anchor Positioning" and "Popover" which use pure HTML and CSS
* Baseline - tool to check compatibility
* EsLint - warns anything that doesn't match the targeted baseline version for HTML and CSS files, integration available in VS code and JetBrains webstorm
* You can use "ask AI" in the devtools, make sure to enable "AI assistance" in the settings first
* New APIs: Prompt API for Chrome Extensions, Summarizer API, Translator API, Language Detector API, Writer API, Rewriter API, Proofreader, other soon will support these APIs, built-in APIs that enables you to run AI locally, meaning data never leaves device you can get AI models using firebase also(in typescript)

## IA
* Gemma3n was released - Open source AI model, it only needs 2GB of RAM, available in hughing face, Ollama, Unsloth
* Medgemma - model that can be used in Health apps
* AI-first collab - agentic-first experience that transforms coding into a dynamic conversation that helps navigate complex tasks
* Gemmaverse: you can find fine-tuned gemmini LLM models here
* SignGemma: sign language translator AI model

These models can be implemented in a tool like google collab inside a Jupiter notebook file and using unsloth(a library for fine-tunning LLMs and is very fast and use less memory runs very well in google collab), they can be deployed using "cloud run" with "vertex AI" or "Google AI edge" for local deployments
